{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Operator-delegated rotation plan\n\nThis ticket completes the remaining externally anchored secret rotations from the value_wo state-remediation follow-up. The operator has already rotated and updated SSM for these names, so this task records/health-checks them but does not re-rotate them: `/rebar/prod/anthropic-api-key`, `/rebar/prod/jira-api-token`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password`, `/rebar/prod/gerrit-bot-token`, `/rebar/prod/g2p-github-pat`, `/rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex`, `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude`, and `/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat`.\n\nOperator carve-outs: `github-oauth-client-id`, `github-oauth-client-secret`, and `/auth-solutions/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` are not rotatable by this operator because the needed third-party access is unavailable. `/rebar/prod/gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key` is deferred by operator decision because rotating it would break clients' pinned known_hosts entries.\n\n## Precondition: Gerrit review path\n\nBefore any step that requires a Gerrit review upload/merge, verify the open P1 `deserved-rubidium-pussycat` no longer blocks normal `HEAD:refs/for/main` uploads. If normal review upload is still failing with the missing-tree receive-pack error, do not overwrite production SSM with an untrusted/unmerged public counterpart. Instead: complete only non-merge-dependent rotations, leave the old key authoritative for merge-dependent signing/trust, comment the blocked disposition on this ticket, and do not force-close.\n\nThe merge-dependent step is the op-cert trusted-environment YAML update. The Rebar Bot identity KEY_ADD is a ticket-store operation and does not require Gerrit review, but it must be signed by the currently valid old Rebar Bot private key before that private key is replaced.\n\n## Scope for this task\n\nRotate exactly these five remaining rotatable secrets, one at a time, using the existing provisioning/runbook patterns and never recording secret values:\n\n1. `/rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key`: generate a fresh passphrase-free ed25519 keypair; register the public key as a write-enabled deploy key on `navapbc/rebar` using the `rebar-gerrit-replication` deploy-key convention (unique rotation title if the old title is still present); overwrite the SSM SecureString with the private key; after redeploy verifies Gerrit→GitHub replication is healthy, delete the retired GitHub deploy key. Rollback while both keys are registered is to restore the prior private key from the previous SSM parameter version and rerun the materializer/redeploy.\n2. `/rebar/prod/ci-gerrit-ssh-key`: generate a fresh passphrase-free ed25519 keypair; add the public key to the `rebar-ci-bot` Gerrit account (overlap with old key); overwrite the SSM SecureString with the private key and update the GitHub Actions `GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY` secret so CI vote-back uses it; verify by a real Gerrit Verify vote-back on a harmless/recheckable change or by an SSH `gerrit version` command authenticated as `rebar-ci-bot`; only then remove the retired public key from the account. Rollback during overlap is to restore the prior GitHub Actions secret/private key and keep or re-add the old public key.\n3. `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET`: generate a fresh 48-character value with the existing `openssl rand -base64 36 | tr -d '/+=' | head -c 48` convention; overwrite the SSM SecureString; redeploy/recreate the auth host Lambda per `infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md`; verify the authorize endpoint returns a redirect to Google. This intentionally invalidates active SSO sessions. Because there is no overlap key, rollback would require restoring a prior value from operator-held secret history if health fails.\n4. `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`: generate a fresh passphrase-free ed25519 keypair; while the current old private key is still available from SSM, materialize it only to a 0600 scratch file, build the DSSE envelope over `keyop_payload(\"KEY_ADD\", \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", <new-public-key>)` using `rebar.attest.authorship.sign_authorship`, write that envelope to a 0600 scratch file, and run `rebar identity key add 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d '<new-public-key>' --signature-file <envelope>`. After the KEY_ADD succeeds, overwrite the SSM SecureString with the new private key and update GitHub Actions `REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY`. Keep the old public key registered for historical signatures. Verify with `rebar show unsinkable-varying-pelican` showing both public keys and with a local signature/verification smoke test that prints no private material. Rollback is to restore the prior SSM/GitHub Actions private key; old public trust remains present.\n5. `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key`: only after the Gerrit review path precondition is green, create a separate worktree from current `origin/main`, generate a fresh passphrase-free ed25519 keypair, run `rebar trusted-env add 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65 '<new-public-key>' --root <worktree>` to extend `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, and land that code change through Gerrit before overwriting SSM. After the trust change is merged, overwrite the SSM SecureString with the private key, redeploy/rematerialize `opcert` and `mcp`, and verify `/opcert/health` plus MCP health. Keep the old public key registered for historical cert verification. Enforcement is currently advisory/deferred. Rollback is to restore the prior SSM private key; old public trust remains present.\n\n## Safety / sequencing\n\n- Do not use any `--force` or equivalent rebar force parameter.\n- Never echo, log, commit, or comment secret values. Report only secret names, SSM version numbers, key ids/titles, and health evidence.\n- Use `aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite --type SecureString` for writes, and verify each write only with `aws ssm get-parameter --name <name> --query Parameter.Version` without `--with-decryption`.\n- Use scratch/key material only outside the repository checkout (session artifact directory), chmod 0600, and remove it after provisioning.\n- Before any redeploy/restart that could affect Gerrit, inspect `deserved-rubidium-pussycat` and coordinate with the owner of the Gerrit missing-tree investigation. Do not restart Gerrit or touch Gerrit git data.\n- Prefer zero-downtime consumers: re-materialize SSM secrets on-box with `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh`, use the validated secrets-only autodeploy/blue-green pattern for review-bot and MCP, and avoid Gerrit container restarts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] For each in-scope secret that is safe to rotate under the Gerrit precondition, a new value/key is generated and written to its SSM SecureString; the post-write SSM `Parameter.Version` is recorded and is greater than the pre-rotation version.\n- [ ] External trust stores are updated before consumers switch: GitHub deploy key added, Gerrit `rebar-ci-bot` public key added, Rebar Bot identity keyring extended with a signed KEY_ADD, op-cert trusted environment keyring extended and merged before op-cert SSM overwrite, and GitHub Actions secrets updated where applicable.\n- [ ] Retired overlapping keys are removed only after successful verification: old GitHub replication deploy key deleted after replication proves healthy; old CI Gerrit SSH public key removed after CI vote-back/SSH proof succeeds; old Rebar Bot/opcert public keys stay registered for historical verification unless tooling dictates otherwise.\n- [ ] Consumers are redeployed/restarted with minimal downtime: review-bot/opcert/MCP pick up re-materialized SSM secrets, auth host is refreshed for the cookie secret, and Gerrit itself is not restarted or its git data touched during the open P1 investigation.\n- [ ] Health verification records concrete commands/results for Gerrit reachability, review-bot `/review/health`, Gerrit→GitHub mirror replication health, MCP `/mcp/health`, op-cert `/opcert/health`, CI vote-back via real vote or `rebar-ci-bot` SSH proof, and SSO `/authorize` redirect load.\n- [ ] If Gerrit review upload remains blocked, the op-cert rotation is explicitly deferred before any SSM overwrite and the ticket is left open/blocked with evidence; no force override is used.\n- [ ] Completion comments name the secret names, SSM version numbers, external registration/deletion evidence, redeploy timing, health checks, operator carve-outs, and deferred host-key decision, and contain no secret values."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788819596357399139,"uuid":"a631271d-60b1-4911-ab59-1712bcd657f2"}